ansformation but the first  close-up we get of jen at she-hulk comes  when she hulks out on those skeevy guys  outside the bar this is an incredibly  tightly edited seven seconds check it  out what are you too good to talk to us  yeah notice how we hardly have any time  to take in jen's new superpower form  which is just unusual for this genre  whenever marvel reveals their new heroes  for the first time they love to slow  things down and just take their time  like the mighty thor jane foster and  love and thunder moon night in the  bathroom in episode one sam wilson as  the new captain america in the season  finale of the falcon winter soldier even  kamala khan got kind of a slow motion  leap with her embigent hand in her first  episode but here it's like don't look to  look it's barely two seconds before jen  gets tackled and by the way she gets  tackled by hulk even that happens so  fast it's hard to tell that it is hulk  tackling her but that said the brief  frames we do see of jen the vfx artist  did a really good job with her face her  brow is furrowed and raged little  wrinkles over her nose her head is  sweaty there has been a ton of talk  about she-hulk's appearance her face her  height the musculature of her form the  director kakuro told screen rant that  unlike hulk a character who can look  like a monster she-hulk has to fit into  the human world she goes on dates she  goes to work to pull off creating this  character in this physical space they  used to stand in malia araya who is six  foot seven and when it came to she-hulk  silhouette instead of looking at  bodybuilders they based her on slimmer  yet still super strong olympian athletes  and ballet dancer misty copeland but  there's an added challenge with the  creation of she-hulk space actors like  mark ruffalo and josh brolin have heavy  jawlines and just very specific facial  features that allow them to be mapped  onto a non-human skull and still retain  the essence of their facial performance  but with she-hulk jennifer walters can't  look like a cro-magnon she must retain  tatiana maslany's attractive physical  features and this challenge is  compounded by viewers like us being so  accustomed to seeing female characters  on screen wearing foundation and makeup  smoother surfaces which is a huge  problem when you consider that vfx  artists tend to rely on those kind of  imperfections blemishes bumps wrinkles  and stubble to heighten the photorealism  it's really hard to make just a smooth  surface look photorealistic but again in  this episode they work around it in some  really interesting ways in bruce's  basement lab they just nail the eye line  with tatiana maslany looking up so high  at hulk so that she just looks like his  kid's sister until this one moment when  jyn begins to hyperventilate and bruce  lowers to her level making us think that  jen is about to hulk out in size but  really this is just the setup to the cut  to joke of her just being hungry and  during this scene they have a really  good mix of practical props and vfx with  hulk's binder his massive fingers  flipping through its pages making this  binder a kind of visual metaphor for the  burden of being a hulk for bruce this  thick binder is really just a small flip  book as for him his self-actualization  is complete but from jen's perspective  it is a massive stack of paperwork even  for a lawyer one of the biggest finders  she's ever seen representing how this  coming transition is a major shift for  her now later when bruce realizes jen  does not have an alter ego he tears out  that whole first section of the binder  that you'll notice is labeled alter ego  showing how jen is already making this  burdensome token smaller and more  digestible for her one of the fun things  about the fancy shows are the swords  everybody's got a cool sword and it's  their sword and it's sharper than  everything else and it cuts stuff real  good even the iron throne is just a big  old pile of swords s