es to run him over there's another  good example of maslany in a reflection  over bruce's face notice how it's her  eyes in the rear view mirror directly  over hulk's face little detail here as  they fight jen's thunderclaps look like  a sonic cannon like the kind that was  designed by stark tech in the 2008 hulk  film one thing known to slow down or  subdue the hole now there is a moment  after they hug it out that's a little  awkward notice how jen leaves her arms  outstretched just a little too long  suggesting that they might have directed  tatiana maslany to pantomime hugging  giant shoulders but of course the actor  would have had a reference for how long  to leave her arms up i'm not sure what  to do with my hands like it's not that  big of a deal and really i think we can  chalk it up to this just being an  attorney and a competitive cousin who  would be a bad hugger now the final duel  with titania in the courtroom i think  might suffer the most from this episode  not having enough shots of she-hulk to  work with because really it feels like  an edited montage of a fight than an  actual movie fight we get these chaotic  back to back shots of jen and titania  throwing desks without those characters  really being anywhere near desks in the  shots before a desk falls on titania but  we never see her crawl out from under  that desk just a shot of her randomly  leaping into a jump kick a kick that  must miss gen completely because jen  does not even have to step to the side  or turn even to punch titania across the  room so yeah but hey considering they  had to completely reconstruct this pilot  episode i have to hand it to the full  creative team for coming up with such an  enjoyable introduction to the newest  adventure of the mcu and finally someone  who can match the hulk in strength  tatiana mislani is just a natural  superhero and i cannot wait to see her  join the others to take on kang and all  the other threats of the mcu and of  course to watch the next eight episodes  you can follow me on instagram and  twitter at avos follow new rockstars for  more of my visual analysis that probably  looks into the details too closely but  you love it thanks for watching bye  [Music]  you

